JoyrIDE bundles or downloads the following, each under its own licence.
An entry is added here when its binary is first bundled, and every
third-party licence ships in the app (scripts/license-scan.py).

- LÖVE (love2d.org), zlib licence.
- lua-language-server, MIT.
- love-api and LuaCATS definitions, MIT.
- luacheck, MIT.
- StyLua, MPL-2.0 (an unmodified binary, run as a separate program).
- love.js (Davidobot's, MIT), whose `love.js`/`love.wasm` carry LÖVE (zlib) and its libraries, and the `love` iOS Xcode project and `love-android` Gradle project (zlib / as their repositories state), when a build bundles them.
- PortMaster runtimes, as the PortMaster project states.
- Monaco Editor, MIT.
- IBM VGA 8x16 (`WebPlus_IBM_VGA_8x16.woff`) from The Ultimate Oldschool PC Font Pack
  v2.2 by VileR (int10h.org), CC BY-SA 4.0: shipped unmodified, byte for byte, as its own
  file in `public/fonts/ansiapps/` with its licence beside it, and credited in Settings.
  Never subset, convert or inline it.
- Painter (`art-sprites`), Composer (`music-composer`) and Animator
  (`sprite-animator`), ansiapps' own engines, vendored in `src/vendor/` and
  relicensed MIT for JoyrIDE (decided 2026-11-13; the engines' own
  repositories stay proprietary). Each keeps its own NOTICE for what it
  includes from others: Painter's CoffeeMUD data (Apache-2.0, text in
  `src/vendor/art-sprites/LICENSES/`) and the IBM VGA 8x16 font by VileR
  (CC BY-SA 4.0, unmodified, with its licence in
  `src/vendor/art-sprites/docs/fonts/`).
- libogg 1.3.6 and the decoder of libtheora 1.2.0 (Xiph.org Foundation, BSD-3-Clause),
  vendored unmodified in `vendor/xiph/` by `scripts/vendor-xiph.sh` (pinned by SHA-256;
  licences in `vendor/xiph/ogg/COPYING` and `vendor/xiph/theora/COPYING`), to play Theora video.
- Neumetik's players (`midi`, `bgn`, `synth`, `visual`, `tracker`) and
  `nttplay`, the command-line player built from them, ansiapps' own code,
  vendored in `vendor/neumetik/` by `scripts/vendor-neumetik.sh` and
  relicensed MIT for JoyrIDE (decided by the maintainer 2026-11-13, so the
  file preview can play MIDI, tracker modules and music written as text; the
  Neumetik repository stays proprietary apart from `midi/`). Standard library
  only. It includes the Organya editor's waveforms and drum samples (BSD,
  `vendor/neumetik/synth/data/organya/LICENSE`).
- The Benchmark Libraries sample (`samples/benchmark-libraries/`): its code is MIT like the rest. `libs/` holds the curated
  libraries (`joyride-core/data/libraries.toml`) at their pinned commits, each with its own licence file (MIT or Zlib; docs, pictures and
  tests removed; luasteam's Steamworks SDK is never copied). Its one asset, the VGA font, is CC BY-SA 4.0 (VileR), see
  `samples/benchmark-libraries/assets.tsv`.
- Two more bundled General MIDI SoundFonts, both CC0 1.0 (public domain: nothing to credit, credited anyway), found through Fontastik's
  catalog (a pointer only) and checked against the text inside each file: `pocketsongs-gm.sf2` ("PocketSongsGM" by Vini, 671,012 bytes,
  from https://archive.org/download/wbs-full_202412/PocketSongsGM.sf2) and `protosquare.sf2` ("ProtoSquare!" by Yingchun Soul, 364,238
  bytes, a chip-style bank, from https://archive.org/download/wbs-full_202412/Game%20Gear.sf2). Their provenance beyond the files' own
  CC0 text is not known (see their `LICENSE-*.txt`). Which sound MIDI has is the person's choice in Settings.
- The bundled General MIDI SoundFont (`src-tauri/resources/soundfonts/sony-ericsson-p800-gm.sf2`, 334,920 bytes, SHA-256
  4d78a19f…f5fa): Brian Salter's General MIDI patches for Beatnik (2000), as a SoundFont by "DroidLite" (2021), under the New BSD licence
  of Beatnik's miniBAE (https://github.com/heyigor/miniBAE; copyright 2009 Beatnik, Inc). The licence text, the provenance and the
  no-endorsement clause are in `LICENSE-sony-ericsson-p800.txt` beside it; keep that file with the bank. Chosen as the smallest General MIDI SoundFont with a
  permissive licence in Fontastik's catalog (2026-11-14).
- The IO Checker sample (`samples/io-checker/`): its code is MIT like the rest. Its assets are
  listed one by one, with licence, author, source and recipe, in `samples/io-checker/assets.tsv`
  (and as the Asset Library's record in `.joyride/assets.toml`): most are CC0-1.0, made by
  Painter, Composer and Animator and by hand; the tracker modules, the Theora clip and three tiny
  test fonts are MIT, copied from the r3i6nos corpus (the same owner); and the IBM VGA 8x16 font
  (`assets/fonts/vga.woff`, unmodified, with its licence in `LICENSE-vga-font.txt`) and the BMFont
  page made from Painter's atlas of it (unmodified) are CC BY-SA 4.0 by VileR.
  Also `assets/fonts/SourceCodePro-Regular.otf`: Source Code Pro by Adobe, SIL OFL 1.1, unmodified
  (Reserved Font Name 'Source'), licence in `samples/io-checker/LICENSE-source-code-pro.txt`.
- Coding fonts offered in Settings, each Regular and unmodified, as its project published it,
  with its licence in `public/fonts/code/licences/` and credited in Settings
  (`scripts/check-code-fonts.ts` checks each file and licence):
  JetBrains Mono (The JetBrains Mono Project Authors, OFL-1.1);
  Source Code Pro (Adobe, OFL-1.1, Reserved Font Name "Source");
  Hack (Source Foundry Authors, MIT, from DejaVu and Bitstream Vera);
  IBM Plex Mono (IBM Corp., OFL-1.1, Reserved Font Name "Plex");
  Inconsolata (The Inconsolata Project Authors, OFL-1.1);
  Fira Code (The Fira Code Project Authors, OFL-1.1);
  Intel One Mono (The Intel One Mono Project Authors, OFL-1.1, Reserved Font Name "Intel");
  DejaVu Sans Mono (Bitstream Inc., DejaVu changes public domain, Bitstream Vera licence);
  Spleen in five cell sizes (Frederic Cambus, BSD-2-Clause).
